          "file": "proj/code/video_gr.c",
          "originalSha256": "e3385e63e15c8f9bf48f147ee230c1e6a1348752d14e0feb3f7f2b8fc53acf10",
          "patchedSha256": "8e33cf4fe57c07e24271c0711765741616792543d29ad99b9613a17698a271ee",
          "reason": "Clip pixel coordinates at the exclusive framebuffer bounds, bound rectangle extents, and return success from the rectangle renderer. Inclusive one-past-edge pixels wrote beyond the buffer when the original cursor reached the edge.",
          "verification": "Actual Android edge homing SIGSEGV in draw_rectangle; original actual-source pixel/rectangle guard test fails on the inclusive boundary, corrected last visible pixel, offscreen rectangles and adjacent frame guard bytes pass. Evidence build/arcade-100/c/maze-clipping-{red,green}.log."
        },
        {
          "file": "proj/code/mouse.c",
          "originalSha256": "b6a5563f6fc37b4cbdad1df1469b5e8f54bcc225aa6926dce918cb3291dfbebc",
          "patchedSha256": "a60945a4925bf5fd8b0e43fce6a226ef665c29e9eb7b782045925484d05485ee",
          "reason": "Decode the PS/2 sign bit as a nine-bit signed delta. Casting only the low byte to char turns valid large negative movements (-255 through -129) into positive motion.",
          "verification": "Actual Android homing moved right for a negative swipe. Original actual-source full-range packet regression fails deltaX; corrected signed-char build checks -255,-200,-129,-128,-1,0,1,127,128,200,255 on both axes plus cursor and button state. Evidence build/arcade-100/c/maze-packet-{red,green}.log."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
